.Dd June 17, 2026
.Dt OPENOBSERVE-CTL 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm openobserve-ctl
.Nd lifecycle control for the native OpenObserve observability backend
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
manages OpenObserve, the single native binary that stores logs, metrics, and
traces locally and serves its own UI. It replaced the containerized LGTM stack
.Pq Z-134 .
The OTel Collector remains the ingestion front door;
.Nm
manages the backend it forwards to.
.Pp
Local telemetry is disposable \(em short-lived signal for one developer, not a
system of record. The store self-trims via retention and is safe to wipe with
.Cm reinit .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width reinit
.It Cm install
Download and sha256-verify the pinned binary, provision Keychain credentials,
and register the launchd service. Idempotent; skips the download when the pinned
version is already on disk.
.It Cm start , Cm stop , Cm restart
Load, unload, or cycle the launchd service.
.It Cm reinit Op Fl -rotate
Wipe the disposable data dir; the root user is recreated from the Keychain
password on next boot. With
.Fl -rotate ,
generate a fresh Keychain password first. Guards the path before any removal.
.It Cm status
Show service state, pid, and endpoint.
.It Cm health
Exit 0 if the endpoint is reachable, else 1.
.It Cm logs
Tail the service log.
.It Cm config
Show version, paths, and endpoints.
.It Cm creds Op Fl -show-password
Print the root email; optionally reveal the Keychain password.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -json
JSON output for supported commands.
.It Fl -rotate
Rotate the Keychain password during
.Cm reinit .
.It Fl -show-password
Reveal the root password during
.Cm creds .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZDOTS_O2_RETENTION_DAYS
.It Ev ZDOTS_O2_RETENTION_DAYS
Days of telemetry kept before self-trim
.Pq Ev ZO_COMPACT_DATA_RETENTION_DAYS .
Defaults to 3 on home, 2 enforced on work
.Pq Pa .zdots.work .
Retention is a ceiling, not a brake \(em if the store grows, suspect ingest
volume, not retention.
.It Ev ZDOTS_O2_SIZE_WARN_GB
Store-size threshold above which
.Xr zdots-doctor 1
warns of telemetry volume drift. Defaults to 8.
.It Ev XDG_DATA_HOME
Parent of the data dir. Defaults to
.Pa ~/.local/share .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ~/.local/state/zsh/openobserve.log
.It Pa ~/.local/share/openobserve
Data dir (disposable;
.Ev ZO_DATA_DIR ) .
.It Pa ~/.local/state/zsh/openobserve.log
Service log.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1
.It 0
Success
.Pq or healthy for Cm health .
.It 1
General failure
.Pq or unreachable for Cm health .
.El
.Sh PHI SAFETY
Bound to loopback only
.Pq Ev ZO_HTTP_ADDR=127.0.0.1
on a PHI-adjacent machine; telemetry phone-home is disabled
.Pq Ev ZO_TELEMETRY=false .
The launchd plist holds no secret \(em the
.Cm serve
target loads the root password from the Keychain at boot.
Telemetry is scrubbed at the ingest edge by the collector;
do not write raw patient records to prompts.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zdots-doctor 1 ,
.Xr zdots-env 5 ,
.Xr zdots-observability 7 ,
.Xr otel-collector 8
.Pp
.Pa docs/openobserve.md ,
.Pa docs/storage-hygiene.md ,
and the
.Sy /telemetry-volume
runbook.
